.Dd January 25, 2026
.Dt DRIVER_REGISTER 9
.Os Substrate
.Sh NAME
.Nm driver_register
.Nd register a device driver with a bus
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In kern/driver.h
.Ft int
.Fn driver_register "struct driver *drv" "struct bus_type *bus"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn driver_register
function registers a device driver with a specific bus subsystem.
.Pp
It checks for duplicate registrations and name collisions. If successful, it adds the driver to the bus's list of drivers.
.Pp
After registration, the function iterates over all devices currently attached to the bus and invokes the driver's
.Fn probe
callback for each device (if the bus and driver matching functions allow).
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The
.Fn driver_register
function returns 0 on success.
.Pp
It returns -1 if:
.Bl -bullet
.It
Arguments are invalid.
.It
The driver is already registered.
.It
A name collision occurs.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr driver 9 ,
.Xr bus 9 ,
.Xr device_register 9
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn driver_register
kernel interface first appeared in Substrate.
